{"summary": "This is a scientific paper about the comparative biogeography of two groups of plants, Carex phalaroides and sect. Bracteosellae, which are part of the family Cyperaceae. The study uses phylogenomic reconstruction, divergence time estimation, and bioclimatic niche analysis to investigate the evolutionary history and ecological traits of these plant groups.

Here is a summary of the paper in JSON format:

```
{
  "title": "Comparative Biogeography of Two South American Carex (Cyperaceae) Groups",
  "authors": ["A. M.-A.", "P. J.-M."],
