  "methods": ["phylogenomic reconstruction", "divergence time estimation", "bioclimatic niche analysis"],
  "results": [
    {
      "group": "Carex phalaroides",
      "divergence_time": "Pleistocene",
      "ancestral_area": "central Andes"
    },
    {
      "group": "sect. Bracteosellae",
      "divergence_time": "Pleistocene",
      "ancestral_area": "combination of central and northern Andes"
    }
  ],
  "conclusions": [
    "The biogeographical histories of the two groups are identical, but with differences in timing and mechanisms.",
    "Extant lineages in the same regions show notable ecological similarities, suggesting a process of bioclimatic niche convergence."
  ],
  "funding": ["Comunidad de Madrid", "Spanish Ministerio de Ciencia e Innovación"],
  "acknowledgements": ["curators and staff at MOR and WS", "UPOS staff", "fieldwork assistants"]
}
```

Note that this is a simplified representation of the paper's content, and some details may have been omitted or condensed for brevity.", "dataset_name": "A comprehensive database of expert-curated occurrences for the genus Carex L. (Cyperaceae)", "source_length": 102527, "full_source_length": 94877, "num_context_blocks": 1}

